# Never bake these into the image. Two different reasons:
# - .venv, __pycache__, .git, data/, db, guardrails/__pycache__ etc.:
#   pure bloat - Docker installs its own dependencies fresh inside the
#   box (see the Dockerfile's pip install step), so your Mac's local
#   venv has no business being copied in too.
# - .env: this holds real secrets (Supabase password, OpenAI key,
#   Langfuse keys). An image is meant to be something you could push to
#   a registry and hand to someone else (or to Kubernetes) - baking
#   secrets into it would mean anyone who ever gets a copy of the image
#   has your credentials. Secrets get handed to a running container as
#   environment variables at *run time* instead (see the docker run
#   command), never copied in at *build time*.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.github/
.env
data/
*.md
.DS_Store
